%decision LgManagerJSONHasComissionerTypo
  what:    FromJSON LgManager parses the JSON key 'comissioner' (single 'm') for the commissioner field
  why:     On-disk JSON files use the misspelled key. ToJSON LgManager emits 'commissioner' (correct spelling), so write-then-read round-trips will FAIL. Asymmetric: this can only be fixed by editing both the FromJSON instance and every existing JSON file in lockstep, or by accepting both keys in FromJSON.
  affects: 

%decision LineupAndRosterAreParallelRecords
  what:    CurrentLineup and Roster have identical 9-field shape, distinct types, distinct field name suffixes (C vs R)
  why:     Lineup is the active set per game; Roster is the full owned set. Field-name suffix prevents Haskell record-field namespace collisions. Every position-mutating function exists in two parallel forms across Draft and Validators.
  affects: 

%decision JSONFieldNamesUseShortPositionCodes
  what:    FromJSON and ToJSON for both CurrentLineup and Roster use 'C', '1B', '2B', '3B', 'SS', 'OF', 'U', 'SP', 'RP' as JSON keys
  why:     Matches the short-letter convention used in positionCodeToText and positionCodeToOfficialText. Does NOT match the draft slot names (pitcher, catcher, first, second...) used by Draft and Validators position dispatch.
  affects: 


